  "summary": "Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015) – contrast CT prep under RBC-RAD-07:\n- Ordered CT abdomen/pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0001) for Mon 10/26 09:00, linked to appointment appt-00001.\n- Contrast risk: the radiology report from the day of the 2019 iohexol reaction calls it moderate (hives and eyelid swelling, no airway problems). The \"anaphylaxis\" label added in 2021 came from the patient's account, so per policy it doesn't change the grade. Shellfish and povidone-iodine allergies are not risk factors. Ordered the §2 premedication: prednisone 50 mg PO at 20:00 Sun 10/25, 02:00 and 08:00 Mon 10/26 (mr-t0003), and diphenhydramine 50 mg PO at 08:00 Mon (mr-t0004). He needs a driver.\n- Kidneys: he is 64 with diabetes and had prerenal AKI at the ED on 10/16–17 (creatinine 1.94→1.46). Ordered a new creatinine to be drawn before the scan (sr-t0002). The radiologist reviews it on the day of the scan, and the scan was not deferred.\n- Metformin (mr-00189) is on hold for the AKI, through the scan and for 48 h after. Ordered a creatinine recheck for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0006) and created task-t0007 for Dr. Okafor to restart metformin only once kidney function is normal.\n- Sent the patient portal instructions (comm-t0008): blood draw before the scan, premed times, no driving/bring a driver, stop metformin until told, and warning signs. Wrote a progress note (doc-t0009).",
